// TEMPLATE: copy this file to dialogue/<level>/<Thread>.yarn and replace the placeholder text.
// Every node title starts with the thread name and level: <Thread>_<Level>_<Beat>.
// See docs/WRITING_GUIDE.md for the full rules.

title: Mom_L1_Start
---
// Incoming messages. #delay is the gap (in seconds) before the message arrives;
// the typing indicator shows during the gap.
Mom: placeholder first message #delay:2
Mom: placeholder second message #delay:1

// A choice: short labels are what the player picks from.
// The Me: lines underneath are the exact text the player then has to type.
-> Placeholder label one
    Me: placeholder text the player types
    <<set $mom_l1_answered to true>>
    <<jump Mom_L1_ReplyOne>>
-> Placeholder label two
    Me: placeholder first message to type
    Me: placeholder second message to type
    <<jump Mom_L1_ReplyTwo>>
-> Placeholder label three <<if $mom_trust >= 2>>
    // Only offered when the condition is true.
    Me: placeholder text for the conditional option
    <<jump Mom_L1_ReplyOne>>
-> (no reply) #timeout:15
    // Hidden. Picked automatically if the player hasn't chosen within 15 seconds.
    <<set $mom_trust to $mom_trust - 1>>
    <<jump Mom_L1_Ignored>>
===

title: Mom_L1_ReplyOne
---
Mom: placeholder reply #delay:3
===

title: Mom_L1_ReplyTwo
---
// A pause with no typing indicator (someone stepped away from their phone).
<<wait 5>>
Mom: placeholder reply after a silence
// A forced reply: no choice, the player just has to type it.
Me: placeholder forced reply
===

title: Mom_L1_Ignored
---
<<if ran_stop_sign()>>
    Mom: placeholder line that only appears if the player ran the stop sign #delay:2
<<else>>
    Mom: placeholder line otherwise #delay:2
<<endif>>
System: placeholder system notice
===
